+# cargo-deny 0.20.2 has NO severity level for advisories. `unmaintained` is a
+# SCOPE, not a lint level: it decides which unmaintained crates are reported
+# at all ("all", "workspace", "transitive", "none"). A reported advisory is an
+# ERROR unless its ID is listed under `ignore`. Writing `unmaintained = "warn"`
+# therefore aborts the whole configuration with
+#   error[unexpected-value]: expected '["all", "workspace", "transitive", "none"]'
+# and `cargo deny check` exits before it has checked anything. That is exactly
+# the failure the specification describes for the sibling project Vocument,
+# where a licence check accused the configuration instead of the dependency.
+#
+# The intent — "an unmaintained crate must not fail the build, because a build
+# on an unsupported platform may still need it" — is expressed as "none":
+# unmaintained crates are not reported. If the team wants to see them without
+# failing the gate, run `cargo deny check --warn advisories` in a separate,
+# informational CI job instead of weakening this key.
+unmaintained = "none"
 
